```json
{
  "subtype": "predictive_feature_engineering",
  "focus_variable": "department",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "presentation_type",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Categorizes the clinical presentation (acute symptoms, chronic management, injury/trauma, etc.) derived from the visit reason. This is a distinct clinical dimension that plausibly steers routing to departments without restating department directly."
    },
    {
      "name": "acute_vs_chronic",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Onset/temporality of the condition. This carries signal about department (e.g., acute onset -> emergency/acute care) and is not a component or restatement of department."
    },
    {
      "name": "primary_system",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Organ/body-system involved (cardiac, musculoskeletal, dermatologic, etc.). This is the strongest legitimate predictor since specialty departments map closely to body systems, yet it is a separate clinical attribute, not the department label itself."
    },
    {
      "name": "severity_level",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Clinical severity (mild, moderate, urgent, life-threatening). Provides predictive signal for triage/department assignment and is independent of the department label. Overlaps somewhat with existing urgency but adds granularity."
    },
    {
      "name": "population_context",
      "role": "predictor",
      "rationale": "Patient population/age band. Relevant to department (e.g., pediatric vs adult), though it largely duplicates the existing age_group column, reducing incremental value; still a legitimate non-leaking predictor."
    }
  ],
  "n_predictors": 5,
  "predictive_utility": 0.7,
  "rationale": "All five columns are legitimate, non-leaking predictors derived from the clinical presentation rather than restatements or deterministic functions of department. primary_system and presentation_type carry the most department-discriminating signal; acute_vs_chronic and severity_level add triage-relevant dimensions; population_context is valid but partly redundant with the existing age_group column. As a set they provide substantial genuine predictive leverage beyond the original columns, discounted modestly for overlap with existing urgency/age_group and the coarse severity/urgency correlation."
}
```

